From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:28:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] Split idx.wq_b (G6_IDXQ_SPLIT) and the MTP draft's
 replicated GEMVs (G6_MTP_SPLIT)

G6_IDXQ_SPLIT=1: the indexer's wq_b by output tiles on the indexer layers,
published after its tiles, gathered after q_b (which runs in between).
G6_MTP_SPLIT=1: the MTP draft layer's eh_proj, q_a / kv_a / idx and idx_q,
gathered on a draft gather fabric (port + 72). The gather plan is built in
build() in publish order; the fabrics are created after their model is
built. Both default 0; G6_QA_SPLIT alone keeps its collective numbering.
---
 docs/SETTINGS.md             |   2 +
 engine/runtime/g6m4.cu       |  76 +++++++++------
 engine/runtime/rank.cuh      | 176 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 engine/runtime/s2/native.cuh |   3 +
 4 files changed, 179 insertions(+), 78 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/SETTINGS.md b/docs/SETTINGS.md
index 9408251..346840a 100644
--- a/docs/SETTINGS.md
+++ b/docs/SETTINGS.md
@@ -85,6 +85,8 @@ the short version.
 | `G6_MEM_MIN` | 8 | GiB of MemAvailable the boot must keep after the weights and each layer of the KV pool; under it the engine stops with a message instead of meeting the OOM killer |
 | `G6_PF_TR_BM` | 16 | row blocks per CTA of the prefill GEMM on trellis tiles (`k_gemm_tr`) for large launches: 16 (256 rows, 512 threads) or 8. Small launches take 4 |
 | `G6_QA_SPLIT` | 0 | decode: the GEMVs on the layer input, whose weights every rank holds in full, split by 16-output tiles across the ranks, then all-gathered per layer on a fabric of their own (port + 64) before the q_a norm. 1 = q_a, kv_a and the indexer's k and weights; 2 = q_a only, with kv_a and the indexer's GEMVs run in full while the gather is on the wire. Same bits as 0 (an output tile's arithmetic does not depend on which tiles a launch covers). Every rank must set the same value. Main model only (the MTP layer keeps the full GEMVs). `G6_QA_SPLIT_TPC` (1) = tiles per CTA of the split GEMVs, `G6_QA_SPLIT_CPU` (`--proxy-cpu` - 9) = the gather proxy's core |
+| `G6_IDXQ_SPLIT` | 0 | decode: the indexer's wq_b (idx_q, 4096 outputs, replicated) split by output tiles the same way on the same fabric, on the indexer layers: each rank's tiles are published, q_b runs while the gather is on the wire, then the gather. Same bits as 0. Independent of `G6_QA_SPLIT` |
+| `G6_MTP_SPLIT` | 0 | MTP draft steps (needs `--mtp`): eh_proj (6144 outputs, 78 MB replicated), then layer 78's q_a / kv_a / indexer k and weights (as `G6_QA_SPLIT=1`) and idx_q (as `G6_IDXQ_SPLIT=1`), split by output tiles and gathered on a draft gather fabric (port + 72). Same bits as 0 |
 | `G6_GV_MULTI` | 1 | steps of up to 8 rows run the GEMVs on the layer input (q_a, kv_a, the indexer's k and weights) as one launch; 0 = one launch each (same bits) |
 | `G6_S2_ADAPT` | 0 | S2: choose each round's MTP draft count (1..k) from the sessions' accept rates and the S2 step costs; 1 adds ~1 GiB of main-step graphs |
 | `G6_S2_GROW` | 1 | S2: a session below R holds the KV pages it needs now and takes more as its output grows, admitted and grown only while every live session can still reach prompt + `max_tokens` + guard; a session that cannot grow sits out rounds. 0 = every run holds that worst case from admission |
